## Why This Is Asked
Advanced cross-DC TLS and policy debugging is common in production. This question tests the ability to reason about ALPN, ACLs, and mesh gateway routing under load, and to propose concrete verification steps and rollback plans.

## Key Concepts
- ALPN negotiation across Consul Connect proxies
- Cross-DC ACL/Intent synchronization
- Envoy sidecar and mesh gateway routing
- TLS certificate rotation and CA trust

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node TLS ALPN probe
const tls = require('tls');
const socket = tls.connect({host:'payments.vm-dc', port:443, ALPNProtocols:['h2','http/1.1']}, () => {
  console.log('ALPN:', socket.alpnProtocol);
  socket.end();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to three DCs with federated tenants?
- How would you instrument traces to differentiate TLS vs application-layer failures?
